=== Calm Elasticsearch API Server Demo ===

✓ Engine initialized

Starting Elasticsearch API server on 127.0.0.1:9200...

You can now use curl or any Elasticsearch client:

Examples:
  # Create index
  curl -X PUT "http://localhost:9200/products" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d'
  {
    "mappings": {
      "properties": {
        "_id": { "type": "keyword" },
        "name": { "type": "text" },
        "price": { "type": "double" },
        "category": { "type": "keyword" },
        "in_stock": { "type": "boolean" }
      }
    }
  }'

  # Index a document with ID
  curl -X PUT "http://localhost:9200/products/_doc/1" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d'
  {
    "name": "Laptop",
    "price": 999.99,
    "category": "electronics",
    "in_stock": true
  }'

  # Index a document (auto-generate ID)
  curl -X POST "http://localhost:9200/products/_doc" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d'
  {
    "name": "Mouse",
    "price": 29.99,
    "category": "electronics",
    "in_stock": true
  }'

  # Get a document
  curl -X GET "http://localhost:9200/products/_doc/1"

  # Search documents
  curl -X GET "http://localhost:9200/products/_search"

  # Bulk insert
  curl -X POST "http://localhost:9200/products/_bulk" -H 'Content-Type: application/x-ndjson' -d'
  {"index":{"_id":"2"}}
  {"name":"Keyboard","price":79.99,"category":"electronics","in_stock":true}
  {"index":{"_id":"3"}}
  {"name":"Monitor","price":299.99,"category":"electronics","in_stock":false}
  '

  # List all indices
  curl -X GET "http://localhost:9200/_cat/indices"

Press Ctrl+C to stop the server

[Engine] Persist background task started
🔍 Elasticsearch API server listening on http://127.0.0.1:9200

API endpoints:
  PUT    /:index                    - Create index
  DELETE /:index                    - Delete index
  GET    /:index                    - Get index info
  GET    /_cat/indices              - List all indices
  PUT    /:index/_doc/:id           - Index document with ID
  POST   /:index/_doc               - Index document (auto ID)
  GET    /:index/_doc/:id           - Get document
  DELETE /:index/_doc/:id           - Delete document
  POST   /:index/_bulk              - Bulk operations
  POST   /:index/_search            - Search documents

